### File System Server API Testing
### Use REST Client extension in VS Code or import into Postman

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Get API Documentation
GET {{baseUrl}}/ HTTP/1.1

### 2. Create a new file
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files/create HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "filename": "test.txt",
    "content": "Hello, this is a test file!\nCreated via API."
}

### 3. Read file
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/files/read/test.txt HTTP/1.1

### 4. Write/Overwrite file
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files/write HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "filename": "test.txt",
    "content": "This content replaces everything!"
}

### 5. Append to file
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files/append HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "filename": "test.txt",
    "content": "\nThis line was appended via API."
}

### 6. Copy file
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files/copy HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "source": "test.txt",
    "destination": "test_copy.txt"
}

### 7. Rename file
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/files/rename HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "oldname": "test_copy.txt",
    "newname": "renamed_file.txt"
}

### 8. Check if file exists
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/files/exists/test.txt HTTP/1.1

### 9. Get file information
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/files/info/test.txt HTTP/1.1

### 10. Move file
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/files/move HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "source": "renamed_file.txt",
    "destination": "backup/renamed_file.txt"
}

### 11. Change file permissions (Unix/Linux/Mac)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/files/permissions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "filename": "test.txt",
    "mode": "644"
}

### 12. List all files
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/files/list HTTP/1.1

### 13. Delete file
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/files/delete/test.txt HTTP/1.1
